# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In a noiseless simulation, we will verify that the fidelity metric is $1$ "
"for the circuits constructed. In the experiments on the real QPUs, this "
"analysis will provide a clear picture of how well the dynamic circuits "
"perform relative to the unitary baseline implementation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa isang noiseless na simulation, ibe-verify natin na ang fidelity metric ay"
" $1$ para sa mga nagtayong circuit. Sa mga eksperimento sa tunay na QPU, ang"
" pagsusuring ito ay magbibigay ng malinaw na larawan kung gaano kahusay ang "
"pagganap ng mga dynamic na circuit kumpara sa unitary baseline na "
"implementasyon.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Quality metrics {#quality-metrics}"
msgstr "Mga quality metric {#quality-metrics}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To evaluate the success of the long-range CX protocol, we measure how close "
"the output state is to the ideal Bell state. A convenient way to quantify "
"this is by computing the state fidelity using expectation values of Pauli "
"operators. We can compute fidelity for a Bell state on the control and "
"target state after knowing the $\\braket{XX}$, $\\braket{YY}$, and "
"$\\braket{ZZ}$. In particular,\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang suriin ang tagumpay ng long-range CX protocol, sinusukat natin kung "
"gaano kalapit ang output state sa ideal na Bell state. Isang maginhawang "
"paraan upang masukat ito ay ang pag-compute ng state fidelity gamit ang mga "
"expectation value ng mga Pauli operator. Ang fidelity para sa isang Bell "
"state sa control at target state ay maaaring makalkula pagkatapos malaman "
"ang $\\braket{XX}$, $\\braket{YY}$, at $\\braket{ZZ}$. Partikular,\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$ F = \\frac{1}{4} (1 + \\braket{XX} - \\braket{YY} + \\braket{ZZ})$$\n"
msgstr "$$ F = \\frac{1}{4} (1 + \\braket{XX} - \\braket{YY} + \\braket{ZZ})$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To compute these expectation values from raw measurement data, we define a "
"set of helper functions:\n"
msgstr ""
"Upang makalkula ang mga expectation value na ito mula sa hilaw na datos ng "
"sukat, nagtatakda tayo ng isang hanay ng mga helper function:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`compute_ZZ_expectation`**: Given measurement counts, computes the "
"expectation value of a two-qubit Pauli operator in the $Z$ basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"**`compute_ZZ_expectation`**: Kung bibigyan ng mga bilang ng sukat, "
"kinakalkula ang expectation value ng isang two-qubit Pauli operator sa $Z$ "
"na batayan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`compute_fidelity`**: Combines the expectation values of $XX$, $YY$, and "
"$ZZ$ into the fidelity expression above.\n"
msgstr ""
"**`compute_fidelity`**: Pinagsasama ang mga expectation value ng $XX$, $YY$,"
" at $ZZ$ sa fidelity expression sa itaas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**`get_counts_from_bitarray`**: Utility to extract counts from backend "
"result objects.\n"
msgstr ""
"**`get_counts_from_bitarray`**: Utility para sa pagkuha ng mga bilang mula "
"sa mga result object ng backend.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As expected in a noiseless simulation, the fidelities in both dynamic "
"circuits and unitary circuits are $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tulad ng inaasahan sa isang noiseless na simulation, ang mga fidelity sa "
"parehong dynamic at unitary circuit ay $1$.\n"

